 "notes": ["Open seat: John James (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 10th District is an open seat after Republican John James left to run for governor, and it sits on Republican-leaning turf in Macomb County. Christina Hines has outraised Mike Bouchard Jr. and benefits from far more outside spending on her behalf, while outside groups have spent heavily against Bouchard. Governor Whitmer has campaigned with Democrats in the district, and national groups treat the race as pivotal for House control.\n\nMost expert ratings call the race Lean Democratic, though a few keep it a tossup or tilt Republican. Prediction markets price Hines at roughly 73-74 percent, while the limited polling, all Democratic-sponsored, actually shows Bouchard narrowly ahead. The evidence points to a genuine tossup with a modest Democratic edge, and the outcome likely hinges on turnout in a low-information race between two relatively new candidates.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6628, "margin": 2.54}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6491, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6831, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.623, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5903, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6399, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6806, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6694, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7119, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6799, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6842, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6979, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6212, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6272, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6412, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6501, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "